INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41656, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have come to claim your bounty have you?$B$B<Commander Aggnash lets out a hearty laugh.>$B$BYour actions this day may have saved lives within Shatterblade and for that you have my thanks. Your actions are worthy of the Horde, and even more worthy of reward.', 0),
(41657, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Commander Aggnash takes his time, studying the letter with some interest>$B$BIt would appear that the Dragonmaw Clan is not as united as we once thought. This news is relieving to hear.', 0),
(41658, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Commander Aggnash looks on with a slight gaze of disbelief>$B$BYou were successful?$B$B<Commander Aggnash lets out a hearty laugh>$B$BYou have overcome your enemy, you have defeated Korlag! A mighty foe such as him was a dauntless task, and yet here you are, victorious. Be proud in your glory today, for you have done what very few could achieve.$B$BTake this, as a thanks from the Horde itself!', 0),
(41659, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent work, the Sal\'Galaz Mines hold quite a considerable amount of iron ore that should aid our efforts handily. Take this, as a reward for your actions this day.', 0),
(41660, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Glory and honor to your name! You have defeated our foe, and brought victory to the Horde. I have prepared a few items, take one and let it help on your journey.', 0),
(41716, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I saw you speaking with Commander Aggnash. What he speaks is the truth. We are under constant threat from a much more powerful enemy. The Dragonmaw have a grip over the region, and their power is unmatched. They outnumber even the dwarves of Dun Kithas by a significant margin.$B$BIf we want to truly make our place here, we will need to take action before action is taken upon us.', 0),
(41717, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'ve recovered them?$B$B<Advisor Ranagg snatches the orders from your hands, and quickly begins to read.>$B$BThese orders seem to contain plans for further invasions in the region.', 0),
(41718, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So, they do intend to target us.', 0),
(41719, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Commander Aggnash lets out a hearty laugh>$B$BYou have done well this day, Geshgan was a brutal enemy, and now he has fallen. You have served us well.', 0),
(41720, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done well, these have not been tampered by Dragonmaw hands... Go now, for I have research to do.', 0),
(41721, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The day of victory has come at last, your actions have paved the way for the Horde to claim this land for itself. Thrall\'s wisdom is clear in your actions.$B$BYou shall be rewarded for your work this day.', 0),
(41722, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Would you look at the proportions of these?! These recluse legs will make a fine addition to the stock of food I have available. You\'ve done me a great service, and everyone here in town.$B$BTake these coins, and go with honor friend.', 0),
(41723, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your actions speak highly of your honor $C. The Wild Maw were a threat to be dealt with, and your actions has certainly eased our concern.$B$BTake this coin as thanks from the Horde.', 0),
(41724, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I am pleased. To think one would betray their oaths, friends, and loyalties for power sickens me to my core. You have done the Horde a service in rooting out such a vile traitor.$B$BTake this, may it aid your cause even further.', 0),
(41725, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Such excellent craftsmanship, these components will serve me well.', 0),
(41726, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Such fine craftsmanship, you can tell goblin or gnomish hands touched such engineering.$B$BWith these parts I will be able to advance our efforts in Shatterblade Post even further.$B$BI must commend you for your work. Without the components and parts you have recovered this basecamp would be left in the stone age.$B$BTake one of these items, hopefully you will see use out of them.', 0),
(41727, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The power of the Demon Soul is infused within this blood, its power is undeniable.', 0),
(41728, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done well, now we can begin the more arduous tasks.', 0),
(41729, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Such dark, and powerful energy, it shall serve me well.', 0),
(41730, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Far Seer Mothang lets out a deep, and sinister laugh.>$B$BThe Pendant of Uth\'okk, in my hands...', 0),
(41731, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The power of the Uth\'okk gemstone is flowing through my veins... Such power is euphoric!$B$BI am reborn, and I have you to thank for doing all my work.$B$B<Far Seer Mothang lets out a deep, and sinister laugh.>$B$BThe Pendant of Uth\'okk has been sapped of its power, but I am sure you can make some use of it.$B$B<Far Seer Mothang lets off a deep smirk.>$B$BFarewell $C.', 0),
(41732, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Why what is this? Ancient technology from Grim Reaches you say? Such complex and intricate mechanisms...$B$B<Tarwegg takes a moment to inspect the device>$B$BI must say, this is an incredible find!', 0),
(41735, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Torlag sent you? Bah he is always sending whatever fool he can persuade into hunting me local game. It is supposed to be him that is doing it.$B$BHere, take this silver. It was meant for Torlag, but since you are doing his work for him, you can take it instead.', 0),
(41736, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done well, this is the first step on the path to healing this land.', 0),
(41737, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Such foul, malignant energy... The corruption in this land is evident.', 0),
(41738, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The materials have been gathered. You have done your duty, now let me conduct mine...', 0),
(41739, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You inquire about the Flame of Dagnoth? You say Yor\'thegg sent you? You\'re inquiring about dark and evil things, how do I know you\'re not some minion of evil telling me a great lie?', 0),
(41740, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done, you have proven yourself a capable adventurer! You have done me a good deed, and for that I will offer you the information you seek.', 0),
(41741, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Flame of Dagnoth is located in the Grim Hollow?$B$BI should have guessed.', 0),
(41742, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I can feel it, the flames corruption has been snuffed.$B$BYour efforts here are monumental, and without your help I would have been left nearly helpless. In time, the land should heal, and the elements should rest. I shall remain to study this transformation.$B$BAs a thanks for your actions, I offer you a reward worthy of your effort. Go with honor friend.', 0),
(41791, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Stand tall, soldier. Belgrom did well in sending you here. Look around, there is much to be done here.', 0),
(41792, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'That smell...! It must be Slagg\'s famous hog steak! I could recognize that smell from anywhere. It\'s just like how our father used to cook it. Thank you very much, $N. Being so far in enemy territory sometimes takes a toll on my morale. I appreciate you and Slagg reminding me what we are fighting for here.', 0),
(41793, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Throm\'ka, young one. Welcome to Shatterblade Post.', 0),
(41800, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Let\'s hope you gave those restless spirits the peace they deserve. The dead should stay dead, especially ones who fought and bled for their kin.$B$BStill… makes you wonder, doesn\'t it? What twisted thing got into that tomb and stirred everything up? There\'s something dark at work in those mists, and I\'ve got a bad feeling this ain\'t the last we\'ve seen of it.', 0),
(41801, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Who am I? Ah, you mortals and your curiosity. I have been known by many names across the ages, but you may address me as Sarthyss Scaleheart. It is not by mere chance that you have wandered into my domain—no, this meeting reeks of fate\'s design.$B$BAnd as it happens, mortal, I find myself in need of assistance that only hands such as yours can provide. Strange times, indeed, when a dragon must turn to the fleeting for aid.', 0),
(41802, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A dark ritual? A cursed dwarven sorcerer? Mortal, you speak of things beyond your understanding. That is no mere dwarf—it is a skardyn, a twisted and vile abomination, once kin to dwarves but long since fallen into darkness.$B$BAnd if the skardyn walk these lands once more, it can mean only one thing—the gates of Grim Batol have been opened again.$B$BThe noble draconic defenders who once stood vigil over that cursed place have succumbed to madness, their minds broken by the lingering corruption of Modgud. Her shadow stretches forth once more, reaching to taint the world anew. This is no mere threat, mortal—this is calamity given form.', 0),
(41803, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Now you see the truth, mortal—clear as the moon over the frozen peaks. This skardyn sorcerer must be struck down before his vile work can seep further into the heart of this land. His very presence here is no accident; it is the herald of greater darkness, the echo of a curse long thought buried beneath stone and time.$B$BWhatever foul purpose brought him to Grim Hollow, it festers like a wound—and if left unchecked, its rot will spread. These swamps, already choked with corruption, are but the beginning. Mark my words: the magic he weaves will not stop here. It will slither beyond the Hollow... to Dun Kithas, and perhaps even farther, poisoning the land, the skies, the very soul of Khaz Modan.', 0),
(41804, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ahhh... Of course it would be the searing kiss of the Red Flight that could sunder such foul sorceries.$B$BThe Skardyn\'s wards are woven with the brittle cunning of earth and shadow—strong against conventional magic, yes... but against the raw, devouring fury of my crimson cousins?$B$BI should have seen it sooner—fire has ever been the answer to vermin who burrow too deep.', 0),
(41805, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mmh... You have done what was necessary, mortal.$B$BTheir minds are finally still. No more Skardyn whispers. No more chains of twisted magic. Only silence... and the long sleep they were denied.$B$BDo not mourn them. Their fire now fuels our purpose—their last act will burn brighter than their madness ever did.', 0),
(41806, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dragonfire bombs? Ha-HA! Now you\'re speaking my language!$B$BYou\'ve come to the right gnome, friend! Oglethorpe Obnoticus at your service—chemist, engineer, part-time arcanomechanical theorist, and full-time enthusiast of all things that go BOOM!$B$BBuuut let\'s not get ahead of ourselves. Sure, I can whip up a dragonfire bomb—of course I can! But as it stands, I\'m a bit... let\'s say, under-equipped. Supplies, reagents, blastproof goggles—the usual!$B$BSo! If you\'re ready to lend a hand, we just might make a little history together. A very explosive bit of history.', 0),
(41807, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Oglethorpe adjusts his goggles and inspects the materials with exaggerated precision>$B$BOoooh, yes! The powder\'s potent, the framework\'s solid, and the gizmo\'s got just the right amount of whirrrr. Excellent work! These will do nicely—no duds, no rust, no strange gooey residue. Always a good sign!$B$BNow stand back, friend—way back—and prepare to witness engineering brilliance in action! I shall now craft... the BOMB OF THE AGES!$B$B...Heh. Just, uh—quick question before I start the final assembly.$B$BYou\'re not planning to use this in town, are you? Or on, say... anyone I know? Or me?', 0),
(41808, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'In your absence, there has been much disturbance. Strange lights, flickering with unnatural hues, have danced from the depths of that cursed crypt. The air itself trembles with arcane dissonance. Whatever stirs beneath... it grows stronger.$B$BIt is good that you have returned. We are running out of time.$B$BMay the gnome\'s contraption—chaotic though it may be—combined with the sacred fire of my kin, be enough to quell the abomination that waits below. If it is not... then the consequences will echo far beyond these hills.', 0),
(41809, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'At last... the taint lifts.$B$B<His wings flex slightly as the oppressive weight of dark magic dissipates, the air itself seeming to sigh in relief. The swamp\'s murky waters ripple as if awakening from a long nightmare.>$B$BGrim Hollow will mend. The earth remembers how to heal... given time.$B$BYet this victory is but one ember plucked from a wildfire. The Skardyn do not act alone—they are rats fleeing a sinking nest. Grim Batol has spat out more of their kind, scattered like rot across Khaz Modan.$B$BAnd worst of all... they scurry with purpose. This was no mere exile. They serve something. Something old. Something hungry.$B$BMark my words, mortal—this is not over. Whatever they plan... we must find it before it finds us.$B$BAnd next time... the fire we bring may not be enough.', 0),
(41846, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, welcome to Dun Kithas, $N! Truly, it lifts me heart to see new faces in our midst. Dark days are looming over us, no doubt, and every pair of hands shall be vital in the trials ahead.', 0),
(41848, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So... the tales whispered by the dwarves of Dun Kithas held truth after all. Curious. One must wonder just how many hidden, long-forgotten passages into Grim Batol yet remain buried beneath stone and time... and what vile things may have once crept forth from their shadows.', 0),
(41849, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'ve found it... By the Sunwell, I can scarcely believe it.$B$B<Ranger Feallina lifts the crystal, tilting it toward the light. The sun dances across its flawless facets, refracting a cascade of colors.>$B$BThis... this is no mere gem. It is a masterpiece — a testament to craftsmanship long thought lost.$B$BYou have our deepest thanks, $C. We will move swiftly now — the rangers and I shall descend upon the site and recover as many of these crystals as we can... before reporting back to Lord Theron.$B$BYou have rendered a great service to the Quel\'dorei this day, my friend. May the light of the stars guide your path always.', 0),
(41850, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Gemstone of Naraz... Wait a moment—this isn\'t right! Look at it—this isn\'t how it\'s meant to be! It\'s only half of it, see here? It\'s cleanly cut, right along this edge! You didn\'t tamper with it, did you?$B$B...No, no, of course not. That cut\'s far too precise for anyone without the proper tools—or skill, for that matter. Hmm... this complicates things, but don\'t start panicking just yet! I\'ve an idea where the other half might be.', 0),
(41851, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hammertoe... attacked by the Dark Irons, you say? Bah, we were rivals more often than not and rarely saw eye to eye, but still, this news sits heavy on me. I can only hope he found a way to escape.$B$BBut there\'s no time to dwell on that now! The second half of the Gemstone—just as the old texts described! You\'ve done well, adventurer, truly well. Thank you, thank you! I\'ll take it to Ironforge at once. With the right hands and the right tools, it\'ll be restored to its full glory!', 0),
(41852, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'While nothing can bring back our fallen brethren, you\'ve ensured their sacrifice wasn\'t for nothing. These relics you\'ve recovered are priceless treasures of knowledge, and they\'ll undoubtedly deepen our understanding of the Earthen and our ancestors\' legacy.$B$BOn behalf of the Explorers\' League, I thank you, $C. You\'ve done us and our kin a great service.', 0),
(41853, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Groldan glares at the heads you\'ve brought him and spits on the ground.>$B$BHa! That\'ll send a clear message to those Shadowforge rats! It\'s only a matter of time before word of this reaches their so-called leadership. Let this be a lesson to them—think twice before crossing the dwarves of Ironforge, or pay the bloody price!', 0),
(41854, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha! Aye, that\'s me stash, sure as stone!$B$BThought I\'d lost it to those thrice-cursed Dark Irons — but seems the sorry louts hadn\'t the wit to understand how valuable me notes really are!$B$B<Groldan grumbles as he rummages through the pile, tossing aside old tools and scraps>$B$BNow where\'d I put it... Bah, always buryin\' the good stuff under junk... Ah! There it is!$B$BHere — take these potions. It\'s not much, but it ought to serve ye well out there. Consider it a proper thanks from Groldan Blackforge. Just don\'t go wastin\' it on chasin\' rabbits or pokin\' trolls, aye?', 0),
(41855, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'By the Makers, that\'s splendid news! With the quarry back in our hands, we\'re one step closer to reclaiming the mines and restoring what\'s been lost!', 0),
(41856, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Amazing work, $R! I\'ll send the miners in at once. In just a few days, we\'ll be back to mining, and with it, Dun Kithas will see its glory restored once more.$B$BPlease, take this. It\'s been in my family for generations, but now... now it\'s time for it to taste blood again. You\'ve earned it.', 0),
(41857, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah! Now that\'s a job well done, $R. I\'ll see to it that our fishermen are notified—the waters should be much safer now, thanks to your efforts.', 0),
(41858, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The news of the Butcher\'s demise brings a certain satisfaction, I\'ll admit. Hopefully, that\'ll be the last we see of those murlocs. Now, I can finally focus on what truly matters—the war with the Dragonmaw. We\'ve got bigger fish to fry.', 0),
(41862, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Another Alliance adventurer, is it?$B$BGood to know Ironforge hasn\'t abandoned us completely—though I\'d have preferred reinforcements before things reached this sorry state.$B$BAh, don\'t mind the grumbling. I\'m just an old dwarf with too many battles behind him and not enough warriors at his side.$B$BWe\'ve got work to do and Dragonmaw to send back to the dirt. Let\'s not waste time.', 0),
(41863, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha! That will make them think twice before showing their ugly faces again.$B$BThis many Dragonmaw lying dead in the dirt should remind them to fear the Wildhammer Clan. With their numbers thinned, our caravans from Dun Kithas might finally get some breathing room.$B$BWell done.', 0),
(41864, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'ve done us proud, lad.$B$BTo see this banner again… aye, it stirs the heart. The orcs defiled our walls, but they couldn\'t claim our spirit.$B$BWith this flying once more above Dun Kithas, our people will remember who we are — and what we\'re fighting for.$B$BWell done.', 0),
(41865, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done! That\'s a fine day\'s work — the screams of dying Dragonmaw are music to these old ears.$B$BWith their numbers thinned and the keep cleared, we can send a proper unit to reclaim and rebuild. You\'ve done more for the Grim Reaches than most ever will.$B$BStolgaz Keep will fly the Wildhammer banner again, and it\'s thanks to you.', 0),
(41866, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done, $C! With these crates in our hands, the Dragonmaw will be scrambling to keep their forces fed and armed.$B$BAnd no one can say Garlin Redbrand didn\'t do his part, eh? …Even if I did it through you.', 0),
(41867, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Urgh, that smell could knock out an ogre!$B$B<Dorthas winces and carefully takes the leaking samples from you>$B$BExactly as disgusting as I imagined... but unfortunately, also exactly what I needed.$B$B<He peers closer, his expression shifting from curiosity to concern>$B$BHmm. I was afraid of this. The corruption\'s deeper and more complex than I thought. We\'re not just dealing with sick wildlife—something bigger is behind all this.', 0),
(41868, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Dorthas squints at the samples, turning them over in his hands. His expression darkens.>$B$BJust as I feared… this isn\'t some random corruption. This is the Shadow Curse—the same blight Modgud unleashed on Grim Batol during the war.$B$BAnd it\'s still active. Even after all these years, the curse is seeping out, spreading past the ruins. Stone can\'t hold it back. Time hasn\'t weakened it. If no one acts… this whole region could fall. This is beyond anything we can handle alone. I\'ll send word to the mages in Dalaran. They need to know what\'s happening. As for us… all we can do now is keep watch—and pray.', 0),
(41869, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha! Now that\'s what I\'m talkin\' about! You did more with your blade than the whole damn magistrate\'s done in years of flappin\' their gums.$B$BYou gave those monsters what they deserved, and maybe—just maybe—we can walk these roads again without fear.$B$BThank you, friend. My son would\'ve been proud.', 0),
(41870, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Harfig listens closely as you recount the battle. His weathered face softens for the first time. A faint, tired smile creases the edges of his mouth.>$B$BAye… that\'s the news I\'ve been needing to hear. You gave \'em hell, didn\'t you? I can feel it in my chest—like a weight\'s been lifted, if only a little.$B$BI\'ll never hold my son again… never hear his laugh echo through the halls…$B$BBut thanks to you, some other parent might.', 0),
(41871, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, good—another strong back and keen blade.$B$BI hope your travels were light and that you enjoy your stay in Dun Kithas, though there\'ll be little rest here, I fear. There\'s work to be done, and no time to waste.', 0),
(41872, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Mountaineer Lightboots leans in and sniffs the meat with an almost reverent sigh.>$B$BBy the stones! That smell… it\'s glorious!$B$BNow where\'s that blasted cookpot? We\'ll boil some, roast the rest… or maybe dry it to keep for later… Ah, the possibilities!$B$BYe\'ve done more than fill a belly, $R. You\'ve helped lift the spirits of a whole outpost. And believe me, that\'s worth more than any blade.', 0),
(41873, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Historian Sternhand reads the journal in silence, flipping the final pages with furrowed brows. He exhales slowly, then closes the book with a firm thump.>$B$BHmm. I suspected something went wrong out there... but not this.$B$BBrangar was once a proud dwarf. A good farmer. It\'s a tragedy what happened—whatever did happen.$B$B<He gives you a long look.>$B$BFor the sake of his legacy, I\'ll... omit these final entries from the official records. Some things are best left forgotten.$B$BThank you for bringing this to me, $R. You\'ve done a service to our history, even if it\'s a grim one.', 0),
(41874, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Sorgan\'s eyes widen as he takes the worn tomes into his hands, brushing centuries of dust from the covers.>$B$BBy the Makers… I never thought I\'d see this again. This one—Baggoth\'s Testament! It\'s a first-hand account of the siege of Firewatch Ridge! Incredible!$B$BYou\'ve done more than fetch books, $R. You\'ve helped restore the soul of our people. I\'ll be poring over these for days.$B$BWho knows what secrets of the past we\'ll rediscover?', 0),
(41875, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Mountaineer Lightboots taps one of the bricks, nodding in approval.>$B$BSolid stone… good heft to it. These will hold, once the masons get their hands on ‘em.$B$BWell done, $R. You\'ve helped hold the line—for now. May the wall stand a little longer thanks to your effort.', 0),
(41876, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Magistrate Toughhand strokes his beard and sighs.>$B$BI\'m afraid there\'s no easy answer. Sal\'Galaz mines are overrun with troggs—filthy pests—and the miners have been driven out.$B$BWithout ore, the forge falls silent. And without the forge… well, let\'s just say our mountaineers might be going into battle with rusted blades.$B$BWe\'ll have to find a solution. Fast.', 0),
(41877, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Nazgrim folds his arms and listens intently. After a moment, a smile breaks through his stern expression.>$B$BHurdam Toughhand… I haven\'t heard that name in some time. A stubborn mule of a dwarf—but a loyal one. I owe him more than just words.$B$BAnd besides, the folk of Dun Kithas have held the line longer than any of us expected. If not for their grit, the Dragonmaw would be knocking on Ironforge\'s gates by now.$B$BYes. I\'ll send word to the guild. You\'ll have your ore.', 0),
(41878, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Magistrate Hurdam exhales deeply, shoulders relaxing for the first time in days.>$B$BSo he agreed… By the Light, that\'s a relief. This will buy us the time we need.$B$BI\'ll have couriers ready to receive the first shipment. Slatebeard\'s Forge will run hot again, and our defenders will have the steel they need.$B$BYou\'ve done more than you know, friend. Dun Kithas is in your debt.', 0),
(41880, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'By the ancestors\' beards, you\'ve done what many thought impossible.$B$BWith so many of their officers dead, the Dragonmaw war machine in the Grim Reaches will sputter and die.$B$BCelebrate this victory, but stay sharp — the war isn\'t over, not yet.$B$BWell done, friend. The mountain remembers.', 0),
(41881, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Mountaineer Lightboots pries open one of the crates, sifting the grain between his fingers.>$B$BHmm… aye, I\'ve seen fresher grain in my days… but this isn\'t bad. Mold\'s only hit a few sacks. With a little work, most of it\'s usable.$B$B<He pauses, glancing around, voice dropping to a low whisper.>$B$BStill… you saw what that place has become, didn\'t you?$B$BGood job, $R. It\'s better we have this grain than whatever was lurking there. But if I were you… I wouldn\'t speak too loudly of what you saw. Some truths are better left buried.', 0),
(41882, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Magistrate Hurdam Toughhand listens intently, clearly impressed>$B$BBy the forge and stone, you\'ve done more than I dared hope for! The folk of Dun Kithas and the Grim Reaches owe you a great debt. Take this reward as a token of our thanks.$B$BBut don\'t let your guard down yet—there\'s still Dragonmaw scum skulking in the hills, and we dwarves know better than to trust the peace of a mountain too soon. Stay sharp, and keep your axe ready.', 0),
(41883, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Magistrate Hurdam Toughhand inspects the letter with a careful gaze...>$B$BIt would appear that the Dragonmaw Clan is not as united as we once believed. This news is relieving to hear.', 0),
(41884, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Magistrate Hurdam Toughhand looks on with a slight gaze of disbelief>$B$BYou were successful? By my beard, I cannot believe it!$B$BMany long and hard fought battles will have been avoided thanks to your hard work. The dwarves of Dun Kithas are forever in your favor! Please, take one of these items, as a reward from all of us here.', 0),
(41885, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha! Look at ye, not even half-chewed! That\'s a fine bit of croc-clearing you\'ve done, friend.$B$BMaybe now I can cast a line without losing a toe. Or a whole leg. Or me sanity!$B$B…Actually, forget that last one.', 0),
(41886, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You actually did it? Thank the ancestors. That should make things safer for now—though I still don\'t trust the quiet out here.$B$BAppreciate your help. Not many brave enough to walk into those webs and walk back out again.', 0),
(41893, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Sorgan Trustgrip takes his time to inspect the tome, giving it a mighty blow which sends dust about the library haphazardly.>', 0),
(41894, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Would you look at this baby? Chromatic powered turbo charged goodness! This thing will do wonders in getting me back on my feet.$B$BI scrounged up what I could as a reward, it isn\'t much, but I hope it\'ll work as payment. Now, get lost, I got some tinkerin\' to do.', 0),
(41734, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What is that you\'ve brought, some sort of mechanical gizmo? I\'d suggest you take that to a gnome, they know quite a lot more than the likes of me...$B$B<Jarkal takes a moment to study the mechanism>$B$BWhy, this be some of that Uldaman technology, not some gnomish trinket. I\'ve seen something like this before here in the Badlands.', 0);
INSERT INTO `quest_request_items` (`ID`, `EmoteOnComplete`, `EmoteOnIncomplete`, `CompletionText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41656, 0, 0, 'What can I do for you $C?', 0),
(41657, 0, 0, 'What is it that you bring?', 0),
(41658, 0, 0, 'Preparation will be required if you desire success in the battle to come.', 0),
(41659, 0, 0, 'How goes your progress $C?', 0),
(41660, 0, 0, 'Have you returned with the signets?', 0),
(41716, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(41717, 0, 0, 'Our security is in jeopardy every minute that you waste.', 0),
(41718, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(41719, 0, 0, 'Geshgan Blackhollow is a cunning foe, do not let your guard down.', 0),
(41720, 0, 0, 'Have you recovered the documents?', 0),
(41721, 0, 0, 'Our victory is at hand, make your way to Zarm\'geth Stronghold!', 0),
(41722, 0, 0, 'Have you had any luck in finding those juicy legs?', 0),
(41723, 0, 0, 'What can I do for you $C?', 0),
(41724, 0, 0, 'Have you found the traitor?', 0),
(41725, 0, 0, 'Have you recovered the Dark Iron Components, or are you just stopping by to say hello?', 0),
(41726, 0, 0, 'Have you found the wrecks?', 0),
(41727, 0, 0, 'The blood is required for my rituals, has it been obtained $C?', 0),
(41728, 0, 0, 'Have you gathered what I have asked for?', 0),
(41729, 0, 0, 'Has my task been completed?', 0),
(41730, 0, 0, 'Have you reclaimed the Pendant of Uth\'okk for the Horde?', 0),
(41731, 0, 0, '<Far Seer Mothang is lost in harmony.>', 0),
(41732, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(41735, 0, 0, 'Can I help you?', 0),
(41736, 0, 0, 'Have you gathered the Reachroot?', 0),
(41737, 0, 0, 'Has your task been completed?', 0),
(41738, 0, 0, 'The land yearns for peace, and it is our responsibility to comply.', 0),
(41739, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(41740, 0, 0, 'Has the scale been acquired?', 0),
(41741, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(41742, 0, 0, 'I implore you to bring allies, for this evil may be to great to handle alone.', 0),
(41792, 0, 0, 'Don\'t cause trouble around here, we\'ve got our hands full already.', 0),
(41800, 0, 0, 'Careful out there—Grim Hollow\'s not the kind of place you just stroll through. The mist hangs thick, and the shadows feel... off, like they\'re watching you. Plenty of brave folks have gone in thinking they\'d be fine—most never came back. Would be a damn shame if you ended up buried with the Wildhammer dead instead of helping them.', 0),
(41801, 0, 0, 'A mortal? Here? Speak your mind quickly.', 0),
(41802, 0, 0, 'I cannot say what horrors await you in the depths of the Tomb of Ancestors. The corruption that festers there is ancient and powerful, far beyond the reckoning of most mortals. Prepare yourself well before you venture forth, and heed this warning—do not let foolish heroics guide your actions. Caution and wisdom will serve you far better than reckless bravery.', 0),
(41803, 0, 0, 'Dire times indeed.', 0),
(41804, 0, 0, 'While you seek their knowledge, I shall reach out to my dragonflight. Perhaps among our ancient scrolls and hidden memories, we can uncover some forgotten truth. But hurry. The shadows grow bold, and time is not our ally.', 0),
(41805, 0, 0, 'The whelps are no use to us- you must find the adult kin.', 0),
(41806, 0, 0, 'What is it? I\'m rather busy!', 0),
(41807, 0, 0, 'Got the materials? Hurry!', 0),
(41808, 0, 0, 'You have finally returned, mortal. I hope you bear good tidings.', 0),
(41809, 0, 0, 'Time is of the essence.', 0),
(41846, 0, 0, 'A newcomer in Dun Kithas! Welcome, welcome.', 0),
(41848, 0, 0, 'Be wary. These lands are teeming with Dragonmaw orcs.', 0),
(41849, 0, 0, 'Is there truly no hope left for our kin?', 0),
(41850, 0, 0, 'I must have it!', 0),
(41851, 0, 0, 'Hammertoe probably set up camp close to Angor Fortress. That\'s what I would do, at least. The place is well known for its ancient relics.', 0),
(41852, 0, 0, 'I beg you, adventurer! Time is of the essence.', 0),
(41853, 0, 0, 'Vengeance!', 0),
(41854, 0, 0, 'What is it?', 0),
(41855, 0, 0, 'I hold no grudge against the Magistrate. I understand that the Dragonmaw threat is more important than the mines.', 0),
(41856, 0, 0, 'We dug too deep... too greedily. Now we\'re paying the price for our folly.', 0),
(41857, 0, 0, 'Where do those murlocs even come from...', 0),
(41858, 0, 0, 'And to think that I used to love fish...', 0),
(41862, 0, 0, 'Aye?', 0),
(41863, 0, 0, 'I\'ve sent a sizeable patrol to investigate what\'s left of Stolgaz Keep... but I haven\'t heard a word since.', 0),
(41864, 0, 0, 'I\'ll not rest easy until that banner is back where it belongs.', 0),
(41865, 0, 0, 'Stolgaz Keep was named after my grandfather. I\'ll not see it left to rot under orc boots.', 0),
(41866, 0, 0, 'Be careful—Geth\'kar is heavily fortified. I\'m not joking!', 0),
(41867, 0, 0, 'Be careful out there. The oozes might not look like much, but they\'re not the only twisted things lurking in the dark.', 0),
(41868, 0, 0, 'Wish I could go with you, but... well, I learned the hard way I\'m better with books than blades.', 0),
(41869, 0, 0, 'My lad\'s blood cries out for justice. Don\'t come back until you\'ve made those beasts pay.', 0),
(41870, 0, 0, 'Foul beasts.', 0),
(41871, 0, 0, 'Welcome!', 0),
(41872, 0, 0, 'I would do anything for a proper feast.', 0),
(41873, 0, 0, 'What is it? You found it at Brangar\'s old farmstead?', 0),
(41874, 0, 0, 'Did you make it to Stolgaz? Any sign of the archives?', 0),
(41875, 0, 0, 'There\'s rubble and ruin aplenty out there. We just need to be smart enough to use it.', 0),
(41876, 0, 0, 'You\'ve come from Slatebeard\'s Forge, have you? I feared this moment would come.', 0),
(41877, 0, 0, 'What business brings you from Dun Kithas?', 0),
(41878, 0, 0, 'Did you speak to Nazgrim? Please tell me he agreed.', 0),
(41880, 0, 0, 'Zarm\'geth is no place for lone wolves. Rally your allies and show those orcs the fury of the Alliance!', 0),
(41881, 0, 0, 'Be careful out there…$B$BScouts say Brangar\'s Folly is home to darker things now than orcs.', 0),
(41882, 0, 0, 'Have you been any assistance to Steelwind?', 0),
(41883, 0, 0, 'What is it that you bring?', 0),
(41884, 0, 0, 'Preparation will be required if you desire success in the battle to come.', 0),
(41885, 0, 0, 'You still alive? Or did the crocs drag you under too?', 0),
(41886, 0, 0, 'Still alive? I mean—ah, back already? No? Then keep your eyes open, and your boots dry...', 0),
(41893, 0, 0, 'What is it that you bring?', 0),
(41894, 0, 0, 'What can I do for you $C?', 0),
(41734, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0);
